    {
      "id": 59438,
      "name": "Katsue",
      "username": "Katsue",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-10T22:38:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"j1hopki1\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> j1hopki1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why does it matter for Imminent Destruction?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Because Imminent Destruction is a One-Shot Jinx that does damage when Kismet has her Talisman (Unlucky Break only does damage when Kismet doesn't have her Talisman), so if she has her Talisman, she gets +1 to damage while Imminent Destruction is in play.</p>\n<p>e.g. On turn 1, with no Environment cards or other Jinx cards in play, Kismet would deal each Hero Target 2 projectile damage (0 Environment cards destroyed, +1 from card text, +1 from Talisman damage bonus).</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:35:14.269Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
